  "equipment_type": "Rooftop unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Lennox commercial rooftop units built with the CORE Unit Controller.",
  "summary": "The CORE Unit Controller has BACnet IP (two RJ-45 ports with a built-in switch) and BACnet MS/TP on board, so no add-on card is needed. The BAS writes occupancy, setpoints and network sensor values to Analog Outputs and Analog Values and reads status from Analog Inputs, a few character-string values and multistate values. Commands are not stored through a reset and must be rewritten regularly, or the unit treats the network as offline.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "2 on MS/TP; last octet of the IP address on BACnet IP",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "AI253-AI264 (Current Error, Error Pointer, Most recent Error 1-10) and AI200-AI210 (IMC Version) are legacy; Lennox says to use CSV302 and the device object's version properties for new jobs.",
    "AO123-AO126 (duct static, building static and discharge air setpoints) only act in the matching unit configuration (CAV bypass or multi-zone VAV, power exhaust with building pressure control, discharge air control).",
    "The guide's object tables list Present_Value as optionally writable for the CSV and MSV objects, but its quick start calls MSV310 and the status objects read-only; they report status, so they are shown read-only here.",
    "The controller also has obsolete Lennox proprietary objects (compressor, blower, heating, economizer, air sensors) with no instance list; they are not included.",
    "The guide contradicts itself on COV: it says COV works from firmware 9.01.0144, and elsewhere that COV is not supported."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Lennox CORE Unit Controller BACnet Setup Guide",
    "doc_number": "508112-02",
    "revision_date": "05/2026",
    "url": "https://www.lennox.com/dA/bfb1627cbc/508112-02e.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Run the Network Setup Wizard in the CORE service app (RTU MENU > NETWORK INTEGRATION), pick BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP and choose Room Sensor control mode, which is the mode Lennox recommends for BACnet. The BAS then writes occupancy on AO104, setpoints on AV130-133 (or AO109 + AO110), and space temperature, RH and CO2 on AO113, AO112 and AO111 when those sources are set to Network. Multi-zone VAV units also take discharge air setpoints on AO125/AO126 and duct static on AO123.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AO 104",
        "name": "Occupancy Scheduler Control",
        "why": "0 = occupied, 1-255 = unoccupied; rewrite every 2 min"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 101",
        "name": "Application Mode Control",
        "why": "Mode command (0 = auto, 6 = off)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 130",
        "name": "Heating Occupied Setpoint",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, 40-95 °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 131",
        "name": "Cooling Occupied Setpoint",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, 40-95 °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 132",
        "name": "Heating Unoccupied Setpoint",
        "why": "Unoccupied heating setpoint, 40-95 °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 133",
        "name": "Cooling Unoccupied Setpoint",
        "why": "Unoccupied cooling setpoint, 40-95 °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 113",
        "name": "Space Temperature Input",
        "why": "Network space temperature; rewrite every 2 min"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 232",
        "name": "Unit Status",
        "why": "HVAC state code: 0 idle, 1 heat, 3 cool, 6 off, 9 fan"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 239",
        "name": "Space Temperature",
        "why": "Space temperature in use"
      },
      {
        "ref": "CSV 302",
        "name": "Alarm Log",
        "why": "Alarm codes, comma-separated; replaces AI 253"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "No BACnet enable point. In the service app, Network Setup Wizard, set the Control Mode: Monitor Only ignores network setpoints and mode demands, Room Sensor uses AO104 occupancy plus AV130-133 or AO109 setpoints, and Network Thermostat takes heat/cool demands on AO101 (values 224-236; Lennox does not recommend it). AO101 = 6 (Off) disables the whole unit.",
    "heartbeat": "The controller must receive a write at least every 15 minutes or it treats the network as offline. Network space temperature (AO113), RH, CO2, thermostat demands (AO101), occupancy (AO104) and setpoints (AO109, AV130-133) must be rewritten at least every 5 minutes if used; Lennox recommends every 2 minutes. In Network Thermostat mode, no AO101 data for 5 minutes puts the unit in its backup mode, and it resets when data returns.",
    "remote_sensors": "Space temperature goes to AO113, space RH to AO112 and CO2 to AO111, with the matching sensor source set to Network in the wizard. After start-up the unit waits 5 minutes for AO113 and stays in a no-run mode meanwhile; after that it uses a local sensor if one is wired, otherwise logs a sensor failure and enters backup mode (code 93). Outdoor air temperature has no network input.",
    "setup": [
      "Default device instance is 2 (or the S-Bus address) on MS/TP and the last octet of the IP address on BACnet IP; it can also be written to AO105.",
      "BACnet IP uses UDP port 47808, which cannot be changed; use a BBMD to reach other subnets.",
      "MS/TP baud 9.6k, 19.2k, 38.4k or 76.8k; default 38.4k. Max_Master defaults to 127 and Max_Info_Frames to 1.",
      "Use consecutive MAC addresses starting at 1, and set Max_Master to the highest MAC on the trunk.",
      "Lennox recommends no repeaters and, above 9.6k baud, no more than 20 Lennox units and 30 devices per router.",
      "Default device name is Lennox_CORE_2."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Commands are not stored: rewrite all control points after every controller reset.",
      "AO108, AO123 and AO124 cannot be returned to the local setpoint once written, except by a controller reset.",
      "AV130-133 are rejected as out of range if a heating setpoint is not below its cooling setpoint by the changeover deadband (Parameter 152, default 3 °F).",
      "AO129 economizer control only works with the economizer in temperature mode (Configuration ID 1, position 2 = T).",
      "Use ReadPropertyMultiple when reading many analog objects."
    ]
  },
